so i am a huge fan of house mark i've  loved their games over the years but to  be honest i did not love returnal when i  first started playing now with that  being said i have since went back to the  game and to be totally honest with you  guys i have truly fell in love with it  it is finally clicked for me and it's  certainly one of the best games i've  played this year and really a standout  on the ps5 which i know that's what the  review said at the time but as i've  gotten older i just don't have as much  time to immediately sink into games  right when they come out and beat them  very quickly like i used to by the way  people of the internet if you are new  here i'm retrorecontour and i'm just a  dad who loves games and the stories they  tell we post videos every week here on  youtube and today we are talking all  about returnal and my experience so far  of thinking that i kind of liked it too  i don't really like this game too  absolutely loving this game so today i  kind of just want to walk you through my  story with the game so far and what my  experience has been like and then if any  of you are kind of still on the fence  about the game or maybe you tried it and  didn't love it and you kind of wondered  should i pick it back up maybe this will  help you decide whether or not you  should and this is some footage straight  from my ps5 a lot of what you're seeing  here is going to be the second biome  there's not going to be any boss  spoilers but there will be spoilers for  various parts of the level so if you  don't want to see anything at all then  you might just want to listen but there  will be no major spoilers in this video  so as i mentioned in the opening i've  been a pretty big fan of house mart for  a while now i absolutely loved rezo gun  it was my most played game on the ps4 at  launch like i just played a ton of rezzo  gun and for a while my claim to fame is  i was actually top 10 in the high scores  on rezo gun that's how much i got into  it and if you haven't played resogun  before it's not really a top down  shooter it's more kind of like a shooter  from the side i'm not even really sure  what the correct technical name for it  is but it's like that old school classic  arcade style of game where you're really  just playing for high scores yes you can  beat the game but after that after you  beat the game it's all about trying to  perfect your run and master it i enjoyed  super stardust enjoyed dead nation  enjoyed outland several of their other  games as well but by far the one that  really stood out for me was rezo gun so  being such a huge fan of house mark i  absolutely knew i was going to play  return on knew i was going to purchase  it for ps5 and was really excited about  this change for them because they  actually put out an article i can't  remember if it was like a blog post or  what it was but house mark put out a  piece basically telling everyone that  they felt arcade was dead and as a  result of that they were going to have  to shift and the types of games they  make were going to have to change in  order for them to survive and i really  thought it was a fascinating piece  because even me as someone who had  played all of their games or almost all  their games rather i could see that they  were never super popular and despite me  loving them so much and recognizing the  immense quality of the gameplay because  trust me guys if you haven't had a  chance to play some of their older games  definitely look back through their  library and give some of them a shot  because the gameplay which at the end of  the day that's really what it's all  about right even when they weren't so  worried about story or anything like  that the gameplay was top notch so i  knew going in that return would  absolutely have top-notch gameplay even  though it was a shift it was going third  person it wasn't that side-scrolling or  a top-down shooter anymore i got it on  launch day actually streamed it a little  bit i've even posted some videos here on  the channel about it and while i enjoyed  it like it just didn't click for me i i  saw the signs i saw little glimpses of  oh i can see house mark's dna in this i  made a video of how i thought it really  compared to metroid especially metroid  prime and when it first launched there  was a lot of talk around the game's  difficulty and i certainly thought it  was a difficult game but to the age i'm  at right now with working on a youtube  channel having a wife kids full-time job  all that stuff i'm really not so  concerned with difficulty as i am  concerned with how a game respects your  time and at least early on i honestly  didn't feel like it was very respectful  of my time because you would just you  know go so far and spend a couple of  hours playing only to have your progress  instantly reset the moment that you die  i mean everything goes back to the  beginning and this is coming from  someone who is a huge fan of the souls  games i've platinum bloodborne i i know  that formula and i'm totally okay with  having to play and learn and get better  and get better and get better or get  good as they say right but for whatever  reason i just was not digging the  gameplay loop of return and keep in mind  this is all taking place in the first  level i never made it outside of the  first level i shouldn't say never  eventually i did make it to the first  boss and i think i beat him on the third  try maybe but after i beat him i kind of  just like like put the game down and  didn't touch it for a while well here in  recent weeks i actually don't even know  what made me decide to pick it up and  start playing again but i saw it in my  ps5 across the menu bar there i was like  you know what let's jump back into  eternal and as i made my way through the  second biome and died and had to go back  through the first biome again it started  to click with me and i started to learn  things i started to pick up on things  that i had missed before and so where  before i thought you know what this game  isn't being very respectful of my time  by the fact that all my progress is  reset instead what i started to see is  no i've been focusing on the wrong  things things that i thought were  important maybe weren't as important as  i first thought because just to give you  an example when i first started out the  game and i think this is how most people  would start out the game you know i'm  going through every single room i'm  opening each chest that i can i'm trying  to kill all the enemies i'm grabbing  every item i'm trying to figure out what  the items even do i'm not really sure  what the best weapons are there are so  many little components of return on  where you're just like how does this  even fit together i don't even know what  this thing does and on a lot of these  things it intentionally does not tell  you there's also a lot of risk reward  with a lot of the choices that you make  and when i say choices i am speaking  strictly in terms of gameplay choices  although this certainly has more of a  story than past house mart games the  choices i'm talking about are not  related to the story at all so i just  don't want you to get the wrong idea  there and there was just something about  when i made it to the end of that second  biome and i finally beat that second  biome boss that i really started to see  even more of that house mark dna and  rather than seeing this as like a third  person action game  suddenly i started to see it as more of  that classic house mark style of trying  to perfect your run trying to make each  run as good as you can possibly make it  and being able to recognize sometimes  early on that you know what this isn't  working out i don't have the right  materials that i need i may even need to  just completely reset this run and as  far as where i'm at now i'm actually in  the third biome now just last night i  made it to the boss third biome by far  my favorite one so far absolutely loving  this one i really should have beaten the  boss but by the time i got to him my  health was so low and i actually didn't  have any healing items at all so i was  kind of like well you know what i'm  gonna go in here and we're just gonna  try this and i think i got a pretty good  handle of how he works and what weapons  might be good for him so next time i'm  already feeling confident about going in  to that fight and it's just such a stark  contrast of when i started the game and  i would die and i felt like i lost so  much progress even though i lost a lot  of the things that i had gained  throughout and not to give away too much  but there are some things that you get  to keep you don't get to keep most of  the things but there are a few key items  along the way as you make it to  different biomes that you will get to  keep but all that being said early on  when i would die after a two plus hour  run it just felt so agonizing this even  though i put a lot of time into it last  night i don't feel that way at all in  fact i'm really looking forward to  jumping back in because of how much i  learned on the last run and how i think  it's gonna help me make an even better  run this next time and that right there  is really for me the gameplay loop of  returnal and what makes it so compelling  and so strong yeah the story is  interesting honestly for me like the  story that i could do without it it's  fine you know it's like an interesting  story i'm kind of curious to see where  it goes at the end but for me it's that  gameplay loop of going into this  completely reorganized area which by the  way it does seem to be randomly  generated there are times where you'll  go in and you'll recognize certain parts  of the level like oh yeah i remember  this but it'll be in a different spot  than how it was before so even when you  go into a room that's completely new  because of the knowledge that you've  gained on past runs and because of your  understanding of the game you feel way  more confident going in i know it sounds  weird it sounds cliche like come on  right like the knowledge gained it's  like no i want items i want upgrades but  it's hard to explain it really is that  knowledge that you get by playing the  game to where you feel truly confident  going in this next time like oh dude i'm  going to absolutely crush this level  this time i've got all the information i  need if i can get a few good drops in  terms of items in terms of weapons we  are going to be set so actually i  haven't beaten the game yet i can't wait  to possibly do another one of these  videos after i've beaten it but i just  wanted to make this one now to kind of  let you guys know where my thoughts are  there may be some others out there who  are kind of on the fence who put the  game away and are like i don't really  get it it got crazy high review scores  and you haven't went back to it i would  say go back to return give it another  shot at least get through the second  biome and then see if things start to  click a little bit more for you they  certainly have for me and i'm really  having a blast with it as always guys  thank you all so much for watching i'll  talk to you again soon
 

